WEBVTT

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:03.900
Back when I was in kindergarten,

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:06.400
I was well-known as the local bad kid.

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:11.620
But that changed after 
I met this older girl.

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:15.620
I loved her like crazy...

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:22.800
But then, one day, she jumped from 
her apartment building and died.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:29.280
She had no one that she could 
talk to about being bullied.

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:33.460
I guess just having an ugly face 
can make you end up like that.

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:35.940
She was a great girl, other than her face.

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:39.270
Makes me glad Iu is so gorgeous!

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:48.190
<b>Tsukinami Ward
Sazanka Elementary School</b>

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:42.440
When I started elementary school,

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:45.450
it was my turn to be bullied.

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:48.180
She's that biker punk Shindou's daughter?

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:51.930
I haven't forgotten what he did 
to me when we were students.

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:55.500
Do you know how much trouble your 
two older brothers caused here?

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:01.820
Sensei, why do you always pick Shindou-san?

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:06.030
I did the same thing the other day, 
and you didn't yell at me like that.

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:07.400
Yeah, really.

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:11.500
My friends were always on my side.

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:14.410
So I learned...

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:17.270
that my friends are my strength.

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:22.260
And that I'm responsible for 
changing my own world...

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.730
To make sure I wouldn't end up like that.

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:33.890
But then...

00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:38.320
If your whole party dies, 
you'll die for real,

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:41.240
but you're the only one in 
your party at the moment,

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:42.860
so be extra caref!

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:46.570
Everything was taken from me. 
My friends, my strength...

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:50.110
All the time and hard work I had put in...

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:53.350
I finally had it, but in one instant...

00:01:53.830 --> 00:01:58.330
I don't... I don't want to 
die in this garbage world.

00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:01.250
No matter what.

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:03.580
So, Yotsuya-kun...

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:12.380
I need your strength in this world 
that has stripped me down to nothing.

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:15.400
Please help me.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:19.870
S-Sure...

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:58.120
Uh... Are you sure this is the place?

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:01.510
Yeah, this is definitely 
the village we saved.

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:04.000
I recognize the buildings.

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:06.580
It's completely fallen into ruin.

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:09.480
Well, if it isn't the heroes!

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:12.850
I never thought I'd see all of you here.

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:16.030
Hello.

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:17.430
What does that mean?

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:21.830
The people of this world can 
identify players at a glance,

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:23.810
and they call us "heroes."

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:25.590
Talk about cliché.

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:29.620
I've been stopping by here now and 
then going on five years now.

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:32.030
This village has always been deserted.

00:04:32.030 --> 00:04:35.950
Does that mean time moves faster 
here than in our world?

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:42.130
<i>I hope that little boy 
is alive somewhere...</i>

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:47.250
What now? We were hoping to 
gather some information here.

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:52.690
Hey, are you familiar with Radodorbo?

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:54.870
Radodorbo?

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:57.270
This is where we are,

00:04:57.270 --> 00:05:00.200
and this is Radodorbo.

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.460
It's on the edge of the continent.

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:04.120
That's so far.

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:06.270
With horses, you could 
get there in 30 days.

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:10.240
On foot, well... I'd say about 
three times that long.

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:12.110
Th-Three months?

00:05:12.110 --> 00:05:15.210
<i>He obviously gave us an impossible task.</i>

00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:18.410
Please, as a favor to the heroes,

00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:20.270
would you let us borrow your horse?

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:22.640
M-My horse is vital to my work.

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:25.630
I really can't spare him, 
not even for you heroes.

00:05:26.290 --> 00:05:27.630
Of course...

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:33.960
Oh, but there's a martial arts tournament 
coming up in the nearby town of Cortonel.

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:35.770
A martial arts tournament?

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:39.700
I believe the reward for the 
winner is three horses.

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:49.480
So winning that martial arts tournament 
is our first goal in this quest.

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:51.490
The timing's just too perfect.

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:54.920
We still have a little time, 
so in preparation for the tournament,

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:57.690
what say we do some 
leveling up on the way?

00:06:00.820 --> 00:06:02.780
Can we really handle this?

00:06:02.780 --> 00:06:05.970
If it's just goblins, they're easy, 
once you get used to them.

00:06:05.970 --> 00:06:08.920
What if some crazy-strong monster shows up?

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:10.130
If one does...

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:11.560
We run!

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:16.030
Yotsuya-kun, what is it?

00:06:16.030 --> 00:06:18.600
Something just moved in 
the bushes up ahead.

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:21.300
Human-sized... They're goblins.

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:22.610
Do we just charge at them?

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:24.440
No, we'll ambush—

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:29.070
They're not just human-sized!

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:30.390
They're actual humans!

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:32.570
Hey, look! Heroes!

00:06:32.570 --> 00:06:34.700
Best prey we could've asked for!

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:36.000
Take 'em alive!

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:38.020
Bandits, huh?

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:44.490
Ow, damn it!

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:46.060
<i>Game Master at your serv.</i>

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:48.630
<i>A human attack has been detec.</i>

00:06:48.630 --> 00:06:50.180
<i>Reducing your experi.</i>

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:51.080
Huh?!

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:52.800
<b>Yotsuya Yuusuke</b>

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:52.800
<b>\h\h\hChef                                   Rank 9→8</b>

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:57.430
Looks like harming humans counts 
as excessive self-defense.

00:06:57.430 --> 00:06:58.950
I lost experience points.

00:06:58.950 --> 00:06:59.590
What?!

00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:01.930
Let's run! Nothing good's 
gonna come from fighting them!

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:05.000
Wind!

00:07:08.830 --> 00:07:10.200
I think we lost them.

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:13.400
Huh?

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:15.690
Where's Iu-chan?

00:07:16.280 --> 00:07:20.200
It's probably safe to assume 
they captured her.

00:07:20.480 --> 00:07:21.690
Iu-chan...

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:23.570
What should we do?

00:07:25.280 --> 00:07:26.470
Help her?

00:07:26.470 --> 00:07:27.610
Huh?

00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:29.380
Wh-What do you mean by that?

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:32.070
Remember what you said 
before, Hakozaki-san?

00:07:32.850 --> 00:07:35.520
That we're all in the same boat.

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:37.390
Right, so we should help—

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:40.450
That's not what I was talking about.

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:45.320
I'm saying the safety of each one of us, 
individually, is irrelevant to the quest.

00:07:46.870 --> 00:07:51.000
So long as any one of us finishes 
the quest, we can all go home.

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:55.520
Giving up when time ran short was bound 
to become an option eventually.

00:07:55.520 --> 00:07:56.740
You get that, right?

00:07:56.740 --> 00:07:59.110
Well, I guess... but...

00:07:59.110 --> 00:08:00.860
Our lives are on the line here.

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:05.530
We should do what gives us a greater 
chance of success, even if only by 1%.

00:08:07.370 --> 00:08:08.850
Hey, um...

00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:11.300
I overheard your conversation.

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:16.100
Iu-san asked you to help her, didn't she?

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:19.940
But you won't go help her? 
Seriously, what's with that?

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:23.380
I <i>am</i> going to help her... 
by finishing the quest.

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:26.360
My internal ranking of the value of our lives

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:29.120
puts Shindou-san at the very top.

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:35.190
And anyone ranked higher than me is 
worth risking my life to protect.

00:08:35.190 --> 00:08:37.110
You're in that group, too, Hakozaki-san.

00:08:37.110 --> 00:08:37.990
What about me?!

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:44.340
So saying that I'd give my life 
to save you guys isn't a lie.

00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:45.790
Yotsuya-kun...

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:51.590
Saving someone's life isn't all 
there is to "saving" them.

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:55.200
Right, which is why I'll 
leave that part to you two.

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:59.020
I mean, I have negative experience 
in that sort of thing, you know?

00:08:59.730 --> 00:09:01.420
Kusue-san, can we talk?

00:09:03.170 --> 00:09:07.390
He's useless! We're the only 
two decent people here!

00:09:09.010 --> 00:09:11.590
Why don't we split into two groups, then?

00:09:11.590 --> 00:09:13.660
I'll enter the martial arts tournament.

00:09:13.660 --> 00:09:16.330
And we'll go save Iu-chan.

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:21.980
<i>So now it's just like last time.</i>

00:09:21.980 --> 00:09:24.070
<i>I'm on my own again.</i>

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:29.990
What the heck is his deal?!

00:09:29.990 --> 00:09:31.170
Um...

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:35.010
When you said we're the only 
two decent people here...

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:35.840
Oh, yeah.

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:38.470
Iu-san is amazing, honestly,

00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:40.730
but it's like she won't open up to anyone.

00:09:40.730 --> 00:09:43.070
She might be trying hard, but still...

00:09:43.070 --> 00:09:47.140
She's pretty, smart, <i>and</i> good at sports, right?

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:48.640
Well...

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:51.490
We kicked off from totally 
different starting lines.

00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:56.270
But there are people who can only 
go to school now because of her.

00:09:56.270 --> 00:09:58.870
For people who aren't good 
at speaking their minds,

00:09:58.870 --> 00:10:01.670
Iu-chan is someone who is dependable.

00:10:01.670 --> 00:10:03.060
Huh...

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:06.030
I bet all the boys do 
whatever she says, too.

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:09.020
Oh, except for him, I guess.

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:10.260
That scumbag!

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:13.370
Just forget about that jerk!

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:16.810
Let's go save Iu-san, 
even if it's just the two of us!

00:10:18.790 --> 00:10:20.520
Yeah, you're right.

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:24.420
Hey, boss!

00:10:24.760 --> 00:10:27.580
Got two more heroes for ya!

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:30.300
Oh, yeah? Toss 'em in the same cell!

00:10:31.460 --> 00:10:33.910
They ended up getting captured themselves!

00:10:34.650 --> 00:10:36.740
I really am on my own...

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:48.650
Busting my butt to kill all 
those goblins was worth it!

00:10:49.370 --> 00:10:52.840
<b>Wizard (Creature)</b>

00:10:49.430 --> 00:10:50.360
Bam!

00:10:50.360 --> 00:10:52.850
Wizard (Creature).

00:10:56.130 --> 00:11:03.800
<b>Yotsuya Yuusuke</b>

00:10:56.130 --> 00:11:03.800
